A[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/fir-against-rahul-priyanka-gandhi-over-assault-during-anti-gyanesh-kumar-protest-in-delhi/articleshow/134780077.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/fir-against-rahul-priyanka-gandhi-over-assault-during-anti-gyanesh-kumar-protest-in-delhi/articleshow/134780077.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T10:30:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Kanchan Yadav</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134780432,imgsize-172516.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘What will it achieve?’: BJP’s Ghosh on Mamata’s Delhi visit as INDIA bloc seeks Prez meet over SIR]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/what-will-it-achieve-bjps-ghosh-on-mamatas-delhi-visit-as-india-bloc-seeks-prez-meet-over-sir/articleshow/134779365.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134779365.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/what-will-it-achieve-bjps-ghosh-on-mamatas-delhi-visit-as-india-bloc-seeks-prez-meet-over-sir/articleshow/134779365.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/what-will-it-achieve-bjps-ghosh-on-mamatas-delhi-visit-as-india-bloc-seeks-prez-meet-over-sir/articleshow/134779365.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T09:46:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Priyanka Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134779365,imgsize-114414.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Few actors possessed his intensity’: PM Modi mourns Nana Patekar]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/few-actors-possessed-his-intensity-pm-modi-mourns-nana-patekar/articleshow/134779336.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134779336.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/few-actors-possessed-his-intensity-pm-modi-mourns-nana-patekar/articleshow/134779336.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/few-actors-possessed-his-intensity-pm-modi-mourns-nana-patekar/articleshow/134779336.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T09:35:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134779446,imgsize-1376180.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pakistan's terror monsters now wreak havoc in its own backyard: India at UN]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pakistans-terror-monsters-now-wreak-havoc-in-its-own-backyard-india-at-un/articleshow/134778978.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134778978.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pakistans-terror-monsters-now-wreak-havoc-in-its-own-backyard-india-at-un/articleshow/134778978.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pakistans-terror-monsters-now-wreak-havoc-in-its-own-backyard-india-at-un/articleshow/134778978.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T09:00:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134779025,imgsize-725374.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NTPC identifies 3 locations for nuclear power projects]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ntpc-identifies-3-locations-for-nuclear-power-projects/articleshow/134778436.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134778436.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The public sector powerhouse, NTPC, has earmarked three strategic locations across India for the establishment of nuclear power plants. Situated in Madhya Pradesh, Bihar, and Odisha, these sites are projected to support a significant capacity expansion of up to 30GW. Feasibility reports have been submitted to the Atomic Energy Commission for thorough appraisal, while NTPC explores potential partnerships with international technology firms to enhance the initiative.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ntpc-identifies-3-locations-for-nuclear-power-projects/articleshow/134778436.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ntpc-identifies-3-locations-for-nuclear-power-projects/articleshow/134778436.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T08:23:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Atul Mathur</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134778475,imgsize-84170.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rupee may be undervalued, markets can be irrational: RBI governor Sanjay Malhotra]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rupee-may-be-undervalued-markets-can-be-irrational-rbi-governor-sanjay-malhotra/articleshow/134777349.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134777349.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[RBI governor Sanjay Malhotra indicated that the rupee is undervalued and the central bank will intervene. The rupee closed at 96.78, down 36 paise from the previous day, hitting a five-month low. Malhotra mentioned that global AI stock corrections could attract foreign capital to India. Despite a robust services trade surplus, the current account deficit has widened due to increased merchandise trade deficit.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rupee-may-be-undervalued-markets-can-be-irrational-rbi-governor-sanjay-malhotra/articleshow/134777349.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rupee-may-be-undervalued-markets-can-be-irrational-rbi-governor-sanjay-malhotra/articleshow/134777349.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T06:44:11+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134777376,imgsize-118540.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Supreme Court to study plea for recall of split verdict on EC appointment law]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/supreme-court-to-study-plea-for-recall-of-split-verdict-on-ec-appointment-law/articleshow/134777320.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134777320.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Supreme Court has agreed to examine a plea concerning a recent split verdict related to a 2023 election law. This law alters the appointment process for the Chief Election Commissioner and other election commissioners. The split verdict occurred between Justices Dipankar Datta and Satish Chandra Sharma on whether to refer the matter to a larger Constitution bench.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/supreme-court-to-study-plea-for-recall-of-split-verdict-on-ec-appointment-law/articleshow/134777320.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/supreme-court-to-study-plea-for-recall-of-split-verdict-on-ec-appointment-law/articleshow/134777320.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T06:37:53+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134777326,imgsize-190972.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Congress protest: Delhi Police to scan videos to identify protesters accused of assaulting personnel; FIR likely]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/congress-protest-delhi-police-to-scan-videos-to-identify-protesters-accused-of-assaulting-personnel-fir-likely/articleshow/134777266.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134777266.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Delhi Police is reviewing videos to identify protesters involved in the alleged assault during a Congress protest. Rahul Gandhi and Priyanka Gandhi were detained for defying police orders while attempting to proceed to Jantar Mantar. Police are also taking action against misleading social media posts regarding their conduct during the protest. Earlier, an FIR was lodged against Rahul and Priyanka Gandhi for forcibly entering Akashvani Bhawan.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/congress-protest-delhi-police-to-scan-videos-to-identify-protesters-accused-of-assaulting-personnel-fir-likely/articleshow/134777266.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/congress-protest-delhi-police-to-scan-videos-to-identify-protesters-accused-of-assaulting-personnel-fir-likely/articleshow/134777266.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-08T06:26:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134777285,imgsize-155188.cms"/></item></channel></rss>